{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent positive bias in downtrends: model forecasts sit ~3–6 EUR above realized levels across most of the 30-day horizon; apply a downward level shift when recent 30d slope is negative.",
    "Trend-lag/underreaction: model does not fully follow sustained sell-offs (it mean-reverts too early), so increase trend-following component when last 10–20 days show consecutive lower lows/lower highs.",
    "Overshoot after rebounds/spikes: after short-term upticks in history, the model projects too much continuation; dampen post-spike continuation and enforce faster mean reversion (cap upside drift for ~5–10 days after a rebound).",
    "Horizon-dependent error growth: bias is smaller in the first few days and grows with lead time; use a lead-time scaling correction (e.g., subtract more for days 10–30 than days 1–5).",
    "Floor-miss during sharp drops: realized prices break below model-implied support levels; widen downside tails/allow lower minima when volatility has expanded (recent large daily moves)."
  ]
}
